<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A conforming HDR Profile (ICC.1 clause 8.10.1) whose only tone-mapping
  descriptor is the pre-rendered AToB0Tag/BToA0Tag pair of clause 8.10.3 c).

  It exists to pin descriptor precedence, which no other fixture can. Clause
  8.10.3 ranks the HAGC tag above a CMM-supplied operator and both above a
  baked LUT, and every other HDR fixture in this directory either carries a
  HAGC tag or carries no LUT - so in every one of them the ranking has only one
  possible outcome. Here the two lowest-ranked descriptors are the only ones
  present, which is what makes the choice observable:

    - icHdrToneMapAuto ranks this build's own operator (the identity of NOTE 6
      of 8.10.2) *below* a rendering the profile author actually baked, so the
      ordinary A2B/B2A cascade resolves the profile and the HDR chain does not
      engage.
    - icHdrToneMapPreferHagc overrides that and takes the HDR chain anyway.

  Reverse those two and the profile still renders plausibly in both cases -
  which is exactly why it is worth a fixture rather than a review.

  The AToB0Tag and BToA0Tag are identity B-curve LUTs. Their contents are
  irrelevant to what this fixture proves; what matters is that the pair is
  present, complete (8.10.3 c) requires the pairing, and 8.10.6 repeats it),
  and that no headroomAdaptiveGainCurveTag accompanies them.

  Colorants, chromatic adaptation and TRCs are the same BT.709/D65 set as the
  other HDR fixtures here, so this profile validates clean.
-->
<IccProfile>
  <Header>
    <PreferredCMMType>ICCD</PreferredCMMType>
    <ProfileVersion>4.50</ProfileVersion>
    <ProfileDeviceClass>mntr</ProfileDeviceClass>
